==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|ang}} {{term|þræll|lang=non}} (Danish {{term|træl|lang=da}}, Swedish {{term|träl|lang=sv}}), perhaps from Proto-Norse ''*þrāhilaʀ'', from Germanic ''*þrāhiloz'', from ''*þreh-'' ‘to run’.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/θɹæːl/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
'''þrǣl''' ''m'' (''pl'' '''þrǣlas''')

# a [[slave]], someone beholden to a [[lord]] or [[master]]

